From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:44:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] The cut labels its edge across a kink inside a cell;
 refuse partial surfaces

_label_cut_edges labelled an edge as the cut's only when both its ends AND
its midpoint lay on the trace. The midpoint test was there to keep out an
edge joining two points of the trace across a turn, but it also dropped
the cut's own edge across a kink of the trace inside a cell, where a sample
has no vertex. add_conforming_surface (which puts no vertex on the samples)
returned every curved surface partial, even sampled a cell apart: an arc of
turn 0.08 rad labelled 5 of 17 edges. At 0.3 cells some came back with no
facet. add_fault hid most of it by pulling a vertex onto every sample, and
paid with snap failures and empty faults (UNFILED 70, UNFILED 22).

The rule now: an edge is the line's when both ends lie on it, they are
consecutive along it (no vertex on the line between their arc-length
parameters), and the edge's chord is at least half the line's length
between them (_CHORD_TO_ARC = 0.5, which admits a kink of up to 120
degrees inside a cell and refuses a hairpin, or two stretches that pass
close). Distances and parameters are measured as the cut measures them:
along chords in the plane, along great-circle arcs on a sphere (a
polyline given with three coordinates on a SphericalManifold).

Measured, old rule against new on one build (10 lines and 10 arcs, both
directions, irregular and regular 1/12 boxes):
- add_conforming_surface: complete 20-22/40 -> 40/40 at 1, 0.5 and 0.3
  cell; empty 0-6 -> 0.
- add_fault: empty 1-8 -> 0; complete up in most rows.
- Hairpins (arms half a cell apart) and a self-approach: no spurious edge
  under either rule.
- add_fault with only its tips and 45-degree turns pulled: 240/240
  complete under the new rule. That pull rule is not changed here.

UNFILED 68's refusal now guards add_conforming_surface too, counting only
the trace's points inside the mesh (points_in_domain, reduced over the
ranks). Its message names the calling method.

test_0898: an arc crossing the box is labelled along its whole length
(fails under the midpoint rule: 0.682 from the trace); no edge joins the
arms of a hairpin. test_0897's empty fixture is now partial, and still
refused. The fault, conforming-surface and line-cut suites (40 files):
428 passed, 1 skipped.

